    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b081ffa2_9e512f47",
        "filename": "board/cheza/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-27T05:36:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Some explanation of the previous solution: the deferred_in_signal is a right-shifted of in_signal. The check of board_is_power_lost() makes sure it is power lost both at this moment and at 350ms before.\n\nBut the deferred signal solution can\u0027t handle multiple short pulses within the 350ms. There is a chance board_is_power_lost() returns true but power lost doesn\u0027t hold 350ms, like\n[1.000] POWER_GOOD -\u003e low, in_signals\u003d0, deferred_in_signals\u003d1\n[1.100] POWER_GOOD -\u003e high, in_signals\u003d1, deferred_in_signals\u003d1\n[1.200] POWER_GOOD -\u003e low, in_signals\u003d0, deferred_in_signals\u003d1\n[1.350] deferred_power_signal_handler() is called, in_signal\u003d0, deferred_in_signal\u003d0, wake chipset task, the board_is_power_lost() returns true. However, the power lost doesn\u0027t hold 350ms.\n\nThe new way of saving the timestamp of POWER_GOOD -\u003e low can check this case.",
      "parentUuid": "b2674bb1_b63075cb",
